Theorem RL-14: Locality freezes a backend-neutral LifetimeBound

  Preconditions:
    - RL-14 consumes the converged Locality lattice value.
    - AIMS freezes a logical lifetime bound and allocation-site identity.
    - Extent and all physical mechanisms remain outside AllocationFacts.

  Soundness property:
    Forall allocation site s, block id b, and Locality L:

      (P1) lifetimeFromLocality(BlockLocal, b) = LifetimeBound.block(b).

      (P2) lifetimeFromLocality(FunctionLocal, b) = LifetimeBound.function.

      (P3) lifetimeFromLocality(HeapEscaping, b) = LifetimeBound.escaping.

      (P4) lifetimeFromLocality(Unknown, b) = LifetimeBound.unknown.

    The result constrains admissible physical lifetimes without selecting a
    VM or compiled placement mechanism.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine over all Locality
    variants. The negative direction rejects any Unknown input mapped to a
    shorter or more precise lifetime.

    Part (P1/P2/P3/P4) - lifetime grid:
      block_lifetime -> block(b)
      function_lifetime -> function
      caller_extent_lifetime -> callerExtent(exact uses)
      escaping_lifetime -> escaping
      unknown_lifetime -> unknown
      Coverage gate: 5 lifetime cases.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY - section_08::verify_rl14_lifetime_facts;
        Locality-to-LifetimeBound derivation)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)
      refinement (SECONDARY - gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-14 by deriving block, function, exact caller, escaping, and conservative unknown LifetimeBound facts without selecting physical storage
